            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DAR01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Erasmus</forename>
                        <surname>Darwin</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1731-12-12">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1802-04-18"/>
                    <occupation>physician</occupation>
                    <occupation>natural philosopher</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">There are only two entries in the diary.  The first is a 'dine at' entry with various
    members of the Wedgwood family, while Godwin is travelling back through Warwickshire after his visit to Ireland, which is a convincing context, and the second is a record of his
    death, on the correct day.  However, he also notes calling on Mrs Darwin when in the Nottingham/Derbyshire area on 13 June 1797.  It is possible that this is Darwin's mother, who lives near Nottingham and dies in 1797.
    
   
      </note>
